{"key": "6f9a7be67d5df869c19a438a", "response": {"id": "msg_011CgAaAqgRDkSMA63Fj37y5", "container": null, "content": [{"text": "**Short answer: none of the option hedges pay if YES. The only clean hedge is the prediction market contract.**\n\nEvery option hedge is flagged does_not_pay_if_yes. The SPY 757/720 put spread costs $566, and your book is still at -$1.2k if YES, worse than doing nothing (-$992). The QQQ spread, TLT put and USO call are the same story. The index only moves about 1% on a CPI hit, so these puts never reach their strikes. They also bleed if NO.\n\nThey protect against a broad selloff, not this CPI print. Their basis risk is that they pay on market moves whatever the cause. The TLT put also relies on bonds selling off with the print, and that correlation can break.\n\nIf you want a hedge against this event, buying YES at 12.5% costs $142 and leaves you flat either way. Want to see how big a broad-market put would need to be to matter?", "type": "text"}], "diagnostics": null, "model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "role": "assistant", "stop_details": null, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "stop_sequence": null, "type": "message", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 8981}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 8981, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 4, "iterations": [{"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 8981}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 8981, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4, "model": null, "output_tokens": 291, "type": "message"}], "output_tokens": 291, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 0}, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}}}
